<title>SPAIN: Bank of Spain sold pesetas against marks - dealers.</title>
<headline>Bank of Spain sold pesetas against marks - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain was seen selling pesetas versus the mark at levels between 84.09 and 84.11, dealers said on Monday.</p>
<p>The central bank declined to comment, true to usual policy.</p>
<p>They added that intervention took place over the course of the day, and at 1610 GMT the peseta was trading at 84.11/4.13 versus the mark.</p>
<p>It opened this morning at around 84.10/4.13.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
